  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Joint Pastoral Porgramme on Colombia-Ecuador Border</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Jointly coordinated by Catholic Relief Services (CRS) and Secretariado Nacional de Pastoral Social (SNPS), this programme structures and strengthens pastoral coordination between four Colombian and four Ecuadorian frontier dioceses to meet the needs of the local population, especially the displaced and refugees. It is an innovative attempt to create a structure that crosses national boundaries to deal with the impact of the Colombian conflict on the neighbouring country. Over three million people have been displaced due to the conflict and around 250,000 Colombians have fled to Ecuador.</narrative>
  </description>
